      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city was originally called Tolt, founded by Americans in 1865, and was renamed Carnation in 1917 after the milk company.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnation%2C_Washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Carnation hosts the annual Sunflower Festival, a month‑long celebration that ends with Sunflower Saturday in downtown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://stateofwatourism.com/explore-carnation-washington/",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The nearby Camlann Medieval Village, a living history museum, recreates an English village from 1376 and opened fully in 2006.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
